& [CanonicalIdentity] is the accepted Phase5 activation authority
  + [canonical_specification_uuid] is 91bb2d88-12d4-4cb7-8d17-3335bc099232
  + [source_snapshot_uuid] is 730d4f89-7573-4c0d-a0a2-cc4cedddd600
  + [conversation_uuid] is cab190f5-eda0-44e0-81a5-51f9605e0baa
  + [requirement_set] is CEB-014 and CEB-015
  + [implementation_language] is safe Rust edition 2024
  + [transport] is local STDIO
  + [activation_state] is active_for_bounded_implementation

& [SingleToolBoundary] is the complete MCP surface
  + [server_name] is cantor
  + [tool_name] is query_sop
  + [input] is one strict ProtocolRequest under a request field
  + [operator_authority] is one EmbeddedRuntimeEnvironment loaded outside the model call
  + [execution] is execute_protocol_request in cantor_core
  + [output] is the unmodified semantic ProtocolResponse projected as structured content
  + [annotations] is read_only, non_destructive, and closed_world
  - never: expose effects, package compilation, trust mutation, model inference, HTTP, or adapter-local semantic behavior

& [ImplementationInvariantSet] is non-waivable
  = must: use the official Rust MCP SDK
  = must: keep stdout exclusive to MCP frames and stderr for diagnostics
  = must: fail startup when the pinned environment cannot be read or decoded
  = must: cap environment and tool request sizes
  = must: reject unknown ProtocolRequest fields
  = must: preserve caller identity, purpose, package bindings, requested scope, budget, faults, proof, continuation, and digests
  = must: make tool failure visible to the model without inventing a successful result
  = must: prove direct-core, CLI, handler, and real-STDIO equivalence
  - never: let the tool caller supply or replace trust roots, package bytes, environment time, or server configuration
  - never: let an MCP SDK abstraction become semantic authority

& [AcceptanceGate] is MCP-AC1 through MCP-AC7
  @ [definition] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\exploded\Cantor_Read_Only_MCP_Adapter_Profile.exploded.sop
  = must: keep CEB-016 through CEB-030 inactive after this slice

